    "created_at": "2019-02-07T20:18:47Z",
    "updated_at": "2019-02-07T20:18:47Z",
    "body": "This doesn't make a lot of sense to me. It seems like pattern-matching on the name, gone wrong.\r\n\r\nHTMLOrSVGImageElement has a distinct usage in the spec, to provide a way of allowing canvas images to be drawn with either an HTML or SVG image element as the source.\r\n\r\nSeparately, folks may be interested in defining some functionality that applies to both HTML and SVG images, perhaps via a mixin. But that's not the purpose of HTMLOrSVGImageElement, and making HTMLOrSVGImageElement into a mixin would break its current usage sites.\r\n\r\nSo, I think perhaps people want to define a completely new `ImageElementUtils` mixin or something. But that's completely unrelated to the existing, separately-useful, HTMLOrSVGImageElement. (It also would be a decent amount of work, abstracting out the processing model for image elements to figure out which parts are common and could be shared, so that any methods defined on the mixin actually work.)",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
    "pin": null,
    "reactions": {
