    "created_at": "2019-02-07T20:57:23Z",
    "updated_at": "2019-02-07T20:57:23Z",
    "body": "I do think it would be helpful to have a mixin for shared functionality, because we want new features like decode or intrinsicsize to automatically be added to both elements where it makes sense, without requiring the SVG spec to always be playing catch-up to HTML.\r\n\r\nBut, if mixins can't be used like a typedef/abstract interface for defining argument types to functions (meaning: this function accepts any class that implements this mixin's members), then we would still need the typedef — and we have a name clash.",
